---
/** Generic disclosures; game identity remains in site config. */
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { hasAdsterra } from '~/lib/adsterra-config';
interface Props { page: 'about' | 'privacy-policy' | 'terms-of-service' | 'copyright' | 'contact'; }
const { page } = Astro.props;
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const analyticsEnabled = !!(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_ID || import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN);
const adsEnabled = !!import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT || Object.entries(import.meta.env).some(
  ([key, value]) => key.startsWith('PUBLIC_ADSTERRA_SLOT_') && !!value,
);
---
{page === 'about' && <>
  <p>{site.description}</p><p>{site.legalNotice}</p>
  <h2>How the guide is prepared</h2>
  <p>Articles link to official store information, developer announcements and relevant community reports. Community suggestions are labeled. Missing or disputed requirements are identified instead of guessed. A source review does not imply firsthand testing.</p>
  <h2>Versions and corrections</h2>
  <p>Each guide identifies its scope and review date. Demo information is kept separate from the full game. Guides are revised for evidence-backed corrections or material game changes, rather than to refresh their dates.</p>
  <h2>Independent project</h2>
  <p>The site is freely accessible without an account. It uses the MIT-licensed <a href="https://github.com/PNGTRID/AnvilWiki">AnvilWiki template</a>. Original editorial illustrations are labeled and do not depict game screenshots.</p>
  <p>Report errors through <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>. Game support is handled by the developer.</p>
</>}
{page === 'privacy-policy' && <>
  <p>This page describes the features currently enabled on {site.name}.</p>
  <h2>Site access and preferences</h2>
  <p>No account is required, and there is no personal-information form. Search runs through a static Pagefind index. Theme preferences and article feedback may be saved in your browser's local storage.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare serves this site and may process request information for delivery, security and performance under its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  {analyticsEnabled ? <p>Analytics is enabled. Cookie-based analytics loads after consent; a configured Cloudflare beacon uses its own data practices.</p> : <p>Google Analytics and the optional Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon are disabled in the current configuration.</p>}
  {adsEnabled ? <p>Advertising is enabled. Configured advertising scripts load after consent. You can decline advertising cookies in the consent prompt; the guide remains available.</p> : <p>Advertising scripts and ad slots are disabled in the current configuration.</p>}
  {hasAdsterra && <p>Adsterra supplies the banner and native ads. Its services may process IP addresses, browser and device information, cookie identifiers and ad interactions to deliver and measure advertising. See <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy/">Adsterra's privacy policy</a>. Ads are labeled as advertisements and are separate from the guide; their appearance does not imply our endorsement.</p>}
  <h2>External services</h2>
  <p>External links lead to services with their own privacy policies. On pages with YouTube videos, thumbnails load from YouTube and the embedded player loads after you press play. Correction reports submitted to GitHub are public; do not include private files, credentials or personal details.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>This page will change if enabled services change. See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> for questions.</p>
</>}
{page === 'terms-of-service' && <>
  <p>{site.name} provides informational guides to {site.game.name}.</p>
  <h2>Use and accuracy</h2>
  <p>Content reflects the sources and versions stated on each page. The game may change, and some requirements remain unverified. Check current in-game instructions when information conflicts. No result or achievement unlock is guaranteed.</p>
  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>External sites are controlled by their operators. Links provide sources or official support; they do not imply endorsement.</p>
  <h2>Attribution</h2>
  <p>Game names and trademarks belong to their owners. The underlying AnvilWiki code retains its MIT license. See <a href="/copyright/">Copyright</a> for the distinction between template code, original editorial work and third-party material.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Report material errors through <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>, with the affected page and supporting evidence.</p>
</>}
{page === 'copyright' && <>
  <h2>Original editorial work</h2>
  <p>© {year} {site.name}. Original text and editorial illustrations are created for this guide. Illustrations are diagrams or decorative artwork, not extracted game assets.</p>
  <h2>Template license</h2>
  <p>The site uses <a href="https://github.com/PNGTRID/AnvilWiki">AnvilWiki</a> under its MIT license. The repository preserves the original license and copyright notice.</p>
  <h2>Game and source material</h2>
  <p>Game names, trademarks and third-party material belong to their owners. Linking a source does not grant permission to redistribute its artwork. We do not claim ownership of game assets or a blanket permission to reproduce them.</p>
  <h2>Rights requests</h2><p>Use <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> with the affected URL and material. Omit sensitive personal information from public reports.</p>
  <p>{site.legalNotice}</p>
</>}
{page === 'contact' && <>
  <h2>Wiki corrections and rights requests</h2>
  {site.contributionsUrl && <p>Use the <a href={site.contributionsUrl}>wiki issue tracker</a> for guide errors, broken links or rights concerns. Include the page URL and evidence. This is public; do not post private information.</p>}
  {site.contactEmail && <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a></p>}
  <h2>Official game support</h2>
  <p>The wiki is independent. For game issues, use the <a href={site.social.official}>official game page</a>{site.social.discord && <> or <a href={site.social.discord}>developer's Discord</a></>}.</p>
  <h2>Contributing</h2><p>Identify the game version and distinguish observed results from assumptions. Reproducible evidence is especially useful for unverified requirements.</p>
</>}
